#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Tool Kits: install the kits for your kind of work and set them up.

A kit is a package `flickos-kit-NAME` whose Depends are what a kind of work
needs (docs/design/flickos-dev.md, ADR-001): Python, Node.js, C and C++,
containers, and the security kits (docs/design/flickos-security.md: network
analysis, web testing, passwords, forensics, reverse engineering, wireless
testing). Nothing is installed by default and this program runs nothing in
the background. It owns no settings and no files of FlickOS's: it installs and
removes kits through `flickos-software` (one installing path: PackageKit, its
password prompt and the plan shown first), and its setup steps change the
user's own files only through the programs that own them, when a button is
pressed (ADR-003): `git config --global` for ~/.gitconfig, `ssh-keygen` for
~/.ssh, `rustup` for ~/.rustup. It never writes those files itself. Four steps
change the computer, not the user's files: the ports that devices on the
network may reach (the firewall), podman's DHCP helper, capturing packets
without root (the user joins Debian's wireshark group, flickos-security.md
ADR-S02) and the wireless adapter NetworkManager leaves alone for monitor mode
(ADR-S08). They are system settings of flickos-control (ADR-003, ADR-006),
which asks for the administrator's password, records the change for History
and owns the value: this program only runs `flickos-control system KEY VALUE`.

Newer versions (flickos-dev.md ADR-007 to ADR-009; flickos-security.md
ADR-S07): a maker's own repository (mise's, Rapid7's for Metasploit Framework)
is flickos-control's system setting upstream.ID too, which adds it and installs
its one package, or removes both. With mise installed, the tools of the
installed kits (USER_TOOLS) get rows: *Use the Latest* runs `mise use --global`
for this account only, so mise writes its own ~/.config/mise/config.toml and
installs under ~/.local/share/mise; flickos-session puts mise's shims on PATH
at login. Nothing is fetched until a button is pressed.

The window lists the kits with a switch each, then the setup steps that apply
to the kits that are installed (a step whose program isn't there is left out).
The security kits are a list of their own under the permission sentence
(ADR-S05), folded until one of them is installed or the window opens on one.
A change shows its plan first (what comes with the kit, or what goes with it)
and asks before it installs or removes. In the live session it says that what
is installed is lost at restart.

The window is a plain GTK 3 window (python3-gi); GTK is imported only when it
opens, so every command works without a display. One window per session
(kits.lock in $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/flickos). Escape or Close closes it.

Text people read in the window is translated with gettext (domain
flickos-kits, /usr/share/locale; docs/12-translating.md). Output other
programs read (`list`, `doctor`) and messages on stderr stay in English,
except the titles in `list`.

Commands:
  (none), window [--kit NAME]
                     open the window, on a kit's row
  list [--json] [--category C]
                     the kits: name, installed (yes or no), title, summary
  plan [--remove] KIT
                     what installing or removing a kit changes (flickos-software
                     plan --json)
  install KIT...     install kits (flickos-software install --json for each)
  remove KIT...      remove kits
  setup git [--name N --email E]
                     print git's name and email, or set them
  setup ssh [--copy] make an SSH key, or copy the public key of the one there
  setup rust         install the stable Rust toolchain with rustup
  setup ports [off|PORT...]
                     print the ports devices on the network may reach, or set them
                     (8000/tcp 3000/tcp 5000:5010/udp; from 1024 up)
  setup dhcp [on|off]
                     print whether podman's DHCP helper may run, or set it
  setup capture [on|off]
                     print whether you may capture packets without root, or set
                     it (from your next login)
  setup test-adapter [DEVICE|ADDRESS|off]
                     print the wireless test adapter's address, or choose one by
                     its device (wlx…) or permanent address, or none
  env list [--json]  the environments: name, kind, kits, running, last updated
  env plan --kit KIT... [--whole] [--extra exploitation] [--json]
                     the sizes of an environment of those kits, asked of its
                     distribution today
  env new NAME --kit KIT... [--whole] [--extra exploitation] [--yes]
                     make one: shows the sizes, asks, then installs
  env update|stop|terminal|database NAME
                     update everything inside, stop it, open a terminal in
                     it, start Kali's Metasploit database in it
  env remove NAME [--yes]
                     remove it, with the commands and menu entries it exported
  env export NAME COMMAND [--menu]
                     make one of its commands yours (~/.local/bin), and put
                     it in the menu
  version list [--json]
                     newer versions the installed kits offer: the makers'
                     repositories (maker, id, on|off, version) and mise's tools
                     (tool, mise's name, kit, yours|computer|none, version, check)
  version maker mise|rapid7 [on|off]
                     print, or add a maker's repository and install its program
                     (mise, Metasploit Framework), or remove both (flickos-control
                     system upstream.ID; asks for the administrator's password)
  version use TOOL [VERSION|latest|system]
                     your own version of a tool through mise (mise use --global):
                     the latest by default, a version that stays, or system for
                     the computer's again (mise unuse)
  version update     mise upgrade: the newest release of the tools that follow
                     the latest
  doctor             what is set up and what is missing

Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 error, 2 usage error.
"""

